@startuml dashboard_owned_packaging
participant Operator
participant "repack.py" as Recipe
participant "Pinned upstream tarball" as Original
participant "Owned tarball + provenance" as Artifact
participant "Dashboard npm graph" as Graph
participant "Offline qualification" as Checks
participant "Loopback synthetic preview" as Preview
participant "Browser peer" as Browser
Operator -> Recipe : build / upstream bytes
Recipe -> Original : verify exact SHA512 / SHA1; bounded data read
Original --> Recipe : regular-file payload
Recipe -> Recipe : change only name/version/CSS value
Recipe -> Artifact : deterministic gzip/tar + complete payload hashes
Operator -> Recipe : verify
Recipe -> Artifact : compare complete expected bytes and invariants
Artifact --> Operator : artifact qualification checkpoint
Operator -> Graph : ordinary file-key dependency; normal lock/install
Graph -> Artifact : existing imports; explicit owned identity
Graph -> Checks : all971 payloads/modes; peers; all package copies
Checks -> Checks : dependency floors; adapter/nine-contract path; build
Checks --> Operator : offline PASS; retained Zod audit finding
Graph -> Preview : unchanged dist; test-only bootstrap
Browser -> Preview : responsive/modal/keyboard/state qualification
Preview --> Browser : synthetic reads; signing/broadcast/outbound denied
note over Browser
  Visual review, hosted CI and release are separate gates.
  No real provider/device/pairing acceptance is inferred.
end note
@enduml
